1. STATUS AND DEFINITIONS

Eri License 1.0 is an independent copyright license based on open-source and
Affero principles. It is not the GNU Affero General Public License, is not a
modified GNU license, and does not claim to be AGPL-3.0.

"Licensed Work" means this Project Omni source code and documentation
identified by this notice, together with releases, modifications, and files
explicitly distributed under Eri License 1.0.

"Licensee" means each person or entity receiving rights under this License.
"Licensor" means Nguyen Ngo and any successor or administering entity
lawfully authorized to administer this License.
"Covered Work" means the Licensed Work and a work that contains, adapts,
incorporates, statically or dynamically links executable code from, combines,
or distributes executable code from the Licensed Work as a combined work.
"Corresponding Source" means the complete preferred form for making
modifications, including source code, build scripts, interface definitions,
installation scripts, container definitions, image build files, deployment
configuration, and other files reasonably necessary to obtain, build, install,
and reproduce the Covered Work.

"Affiliate" means an entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled
by, or is under common control with the operating organization, or a wholly
owned subsidiary. "Control" means ownership or control of more than fifty
percent of voting interests or the power to direct management.

"Business Partner" means an independently operated entity receiving access
under a written, access-restricted, non-resale agreement solely to perform
services for or with the operating organization. A business partner is not
an Affiliate unless it satisfies the Affiliate definition above.

"External User" means a customer, unaffiliated public or private user, or
business partner operating, selling, redistributing, publicly hosting, or
using the Licensed Work for its own independent purposes. A Business Partner
acting only under the operating organization's direction and without independent
rights to operate or redistribute the work is an internal participant, not
an External User.

