13. TERMINATION AND RESTORATION

A Licensee's rights terminate automatically upon a material violation that
is not exempted in writing. The Licensor must give written notice identifying
the applicable Section and violation. If the violation is curable, the
Licensee has thirty days after receiving notice to cease and cure it, and
rights are reinstated upon timely cure.

Rights are also provisionally reinstated if the Licensee ceases every violation
and cure is not possible before notice. Rights become permanently reinstated
if the Licensor fails to notify the Licensee of the violation by reasonable
means within sixty days after the Licensee has ceased the violation, or if
applicable law requires permanent reinstatement sooner. Termination does not
revive a violation or revoke the licenses of compliant downstream recipients.

